Following the structure of ACM curricular volumes, the task force is organizing the body of computing knowledge into Knowledge Areas (KAs). In the draft report, the computing discipline-specific KAs for undergraduate data science are: 

• Programming, algorithmic design, and development; 

• Data acquirement and governance; 

• Data management, storage, retrieval; 

• Data privacy, security, integrity; 

• Machine learning; 

• Data mining; 

• Systems considerations for data mining "in the large": big data, distributed systems, parallel computing, HPC; 

• Professionalism: communication, collaboration, ethics, evidence-based decision making and problem solving; 

• Analysis and presentation: visualization, HCI.

